// reverse an array in place
public static void reverseInPlace(int[] arr) {
    int left = 0;
    int right = arr.length - 1;
    
    while (left < right) {
        // Swap elements
        int temp = arr[left];
        arr[left] = arr[right];
        arr[right] = temp;
        
        // Move pointers closer to the middle
        left++;
        right--;
    }
}

//reverse a part of an array in place java
public static int[] reverse(int[] arr, int low, int high)
    {
      while(low < high)
      {
        int temp =  arr[low];
        arr[low] = arr[high];
        arr[high] = temp;
        low++;
        high--;

      }
      return arr;

Time Complexity: O(n) because the algorithm processes exactly n/2 iterations to handle n elements.Space Complexity: O(1) since only a single primitive variable (temp) is retained dynamically in memory.
